// and open host tool calls (lib/serve-session.ts `SessionLog`) and listens on
// an owner-only Unix socket `<serve dir>/sessions/<id>.sock` (on Windows the
// named pipe `\\.\pipe\gentle-shell-serve-<user>-<id>`) for one server at a
// time, which proves itself with the token in the session's record file. A
// server that starts scans the folder and reattaches every live keeper.
//
// A keeper ends when its Pi exits (its record file stays, marked exited, for the
// server's listing) or when the server stops the session. A keeper no server
// came back to for 24 hours stops its session.

